# Comprehension Debt

All AI-generated Kotlin code must be annotated with `@ComprehensionDebt` until a human has thoroughly reviewed or rewritten it.

- Import: `com.kittenmp.ai.ComprehensionDebt`
- Annotate the generated **class** and **every generated method/function** on that class (the annotation targets only `CLASS` and `FUNCTION`)
- Also annotate nested types that were AI-written
- Prefer the smallest unit that was AI-written (function over class when only some methods are AI-generated; when the whole type is AI-generated, annotate the class **and** all of its methods)
- Fill optional `agent` and `model` from the generating session identity when known
- Do not remove `@ComprehensionDebt` unless the human author has reviewed/rewritten that code
- Modules that use the annotation must depend on `:ai`

```kotlin
import com.kittenmp.ai.ComprehensionDebt

@ComprehensionDebt(agent = "cursor", model = "Cursor Grok 4.5")
class Example {
  @ComprehensionDebt(agent = "cursor", model = "Cursor Grok 4.5")
  fun doWork() {
    // AI-generated implementation
  }

  @ComprehensionDebt(agent = "cursor", model = "Cursor Grok 4.5")
  private fun helper() {
    // AI-generated implementation
  }
}
```
